# Every .env variant is a real secret file. `/.env` alone let two hand-made
# backups (.env.bak.localhost, .env.bak-before-localhost-origin) sit untracked-
# but-not-ignored, and one of them WAS committed. Ignore the family; the
# example is the one exception, and it holds names, never values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/dist
/node_modules
/src/scripts
/build_output.txt
/ticket_types.txt

# ── Developer upload directory (STORAGE_PROVIDER=local) ──────────────────────
# Runtime data, never source. Production uses Cloudflare R2, so nothing here is
# needed to run or build the service.
#
# 93 files were tracked here until 2026-09-12, including customer-uploaded PDFs.
# They are untracked now and remain on disk, but they REMAIN IN GIT HISTORY --
# untracking does not remove a file from the commits that already added it.
# Purging them needs a history rewrite (git filter-repo) and a force-push, which
# is a separate, deliberate operation.
storage/
